From f2856f1cd74414502cf2429dd494150bd18b77ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Alvarado Martinez <45523697+calvarado2004@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep long conversations warm under snapshot-slot pressure

Snapshot slots are fixed at eight per concurrent request, and eviction
retires the least recently used checkpoint. A coding agent's long
conversation shares those slots with its subagents and side queries, so a
few minutes of short requests retire the conversation's endpoint and its
next turn prefills the whole context again, even with most KV pages free
(issue #47).

Evict by GreedyDual-Size over the tokens an eviction loses: each checkpoint
carries the cache inflation at its last use, and its priority adds the span
a request must recompute once it is gone. A long conversation outlasts many
short endpoints, while an idle one still ages out as the inflation rises.

Add --prefix-cache-snapshots N to set the slot total. Rows alias KV backing
and the prepared continuation extent still bounds them, so a large page pool
can retain more endpoints without a re-export.

qualify/prefix_retention.py runs the scenario against a live server.
